// A triplet of eighth notes beams as ONE group — its notes carry their WRITTEN
// (1/8) duration, so per-beat grouping must not split the run where those written
// positions cross a beat boundary (an 8th triplet at beat 3 came out 2+1 with a
// stray flagged note and a bracket instead of a single "3").
title "eighth triplet beams as one"
time 4/4
key c major
part m { section A { c8 c c c tuplet 3/4 { e8 e e } | } }
form main { A }
score main { staff m }
